  "structural_findings": [
    "SNDATA_ROOT contains NO SALT2 x1/c for SNLS, PS1MD or SDSS \u2014 only CFA3 has .FITRES files.",
    "SNLS has NO host mass, NO host surface brightness and NO PHOTFLAG in any shipped file.",
    "PS1MD_Jones18 (1169) is the PHOTOMETRIC sample (SNTYPE==0 for all); the spectroscopic PS1 set is Pantheon_PS1MD_FITS (369).",
    "PS1MD_Jones18 SNIDs (PSc000006) and Pantheon/Pantheon+ CIDs (000006) are disjoint namespaces; naive join = 0 matches.",
    "SDSS and PS1MD SNIDs are both bare integers and collide \u2014 join on (survey, SNID).",
    "HOSTGAL_SPECZ is 0 for every row in both FITS HEAD tables; use REDSHIFT_HELIO/REDSHIFT_FINAL.",
    "Only 4684 of 10258 SDSS rows have any redshift; PEAKMJD is populated for all 10258.",
    "Shipped SDSS SNTYPE counts differ from the Sako+2014 Table 3 in the dataset's own README (499/41/824/624 vs 500/36/907/677).",
    "Extracting on macOS/Windows silently destroys 25 SDSS per-CCD filter curves (44 case-colliding groups, 88 files); CCDAVG pairs are byte-identical, per-CCD pairs are NOT. Case-safe copies shipped.",
    "SNLS MegaCam throughputs are PER-SUPERNOVA (285 filters-<SNID> dirs), not one curve per band.",
    "PS1MD_RS14.SIMLIB covers seasons 2010 + half 2011 but Jones18 PEAKMJD spans 55083-56677.",
    "SDSS_3year.SIMLIB was regenerated 2026-01-27 (NLIBID key added by C. Meldorf).",
    "dscolnic/Pantheon lcparam_full_long.txt names x1/color/3rdvar in its header but all are exactly 0.0 in all 1048 rows \u2014 NOT usable, not shipped."
  ],
  "lensdmu_ruling": {
    "reintroduced": false,
    "note": "No LENSDMU/LENSDMU_ERR equivalent exists in SNDATA_ROOT or in either SALT2 table. Pantheon+ cosmology/distance columns were DROPPED (MU_SH0ES, CEPH_DIST, m_b_corr*, biasCor*, zHD*). JLA e_mb is flagged: its published ReadMe states it includes a lensing contribution and mb is bias-corrected; it is not separable from the table."
  },
